{title: Rock of Ages, Cleft for Me}
{artist: Augustus M. Toplady}
{key: C}
{tempo: 76}
{time: 3/4}
{meta: tune TOPLADY - Thomas Hastings (1830)}
{meta: public_domain Text 1776, tune 1830: both published before 1931 (US public domain); all authors, translators and composers died over 70 years ago. Chords and section layout: original simple arrangement by Tabernacle Tools. Original verses only, no modern additions.}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Rock of Ages, [F]cleft for [C]me,
Let me hide my[G7]self in [C]Thee;
[C]Let the water [G]and the [C]blood,
From Thy wounded [G]side which [C]flowed,
[C]Be of sin the [G]double [C]cure,
Save from wrath and [G7]make me [C]pure.
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Not the labors [F]of my [C]hands
Can fulfill Thy [G7]law's de[C]mands;
[C]Could my zeal no [G]respite [C]know,
Could my tears for[G]ever [C]flow,
[C]All for sin could [G]not a[C]tone;
Thou must save, and [G7]Thou a[C]lone.
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]Nothing in my [F]hand I [C]bring,
Simply to the [G7]cross I [C]cling;
[C]Naked, come to [G]Thee for [C]dress;
Helpless, look to [G]Thee for [C]grace;
[C]Foul, I to the [G]fountain [C]fly;
Wash me, Savior, [G7]or I [C]die.
{end_of_verse}
